translation_en:
I beseech you, Holy Trinity and indivisible Unity, through the triumphant trophy of the most victorious cross and the merits of the blessed and glorious Virgin Mary and all your saints here contained, that you extend to me, wretched and unworthy, and covered with all filth of inner and outer sins, the hand of your mercy, raise, support, and hear my prayer; do not despise but look upon me with your merciful countenance and listen. Increase my faith, confirm my hope, ignite in me the ardor of your love. And because I am unworthy to approach your holy altar, nevertheless I do not seek the recompense of sins but rather feel the piety of your goodness.
Grant this, Almighty Father, who loved man so much that you sent only your Son for his deliverance.
Grant this, Lord Jesus Christ, Son of God living, who saved man from death and did not shrink from the cross;
You are the one who brought back the lost sheep with a pious arm to the fold;
You are the one who prophetically said: "I do not wish the death of the sinner, but that he may turn from his ways and live."
Grant this, Holy Spirit, proceeding from both and poured out upon me in baptism. You are remission of sins, illuminator of hearts, teacher of faithful ones; you reign with one substance and one will with the Father and the Son.
